---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Button from '../../components/Button.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import Mark from '../../components/Mark.astro';
import ProductMockup from '../../components/ProductMockup.astro';
import '../../styles/docs.css';

const colors = [
  ['Paper', '--color-paper', 'page background'],
  ['Paper Raised', '--color-paper-raised', 'alternate bands, chips'],
  ['Ink', '--color-ink', 'text, charcoal band, code bg'],
  ['Ink Soft', '--color-ink-soft', 'body copy, secondary text'],
  ['Terracotta', '--color-terracotta', 'brand mark, large display accents'],
  ['Link Terracotta', '--color-link', 'links, buttons, focus'],
  ['Olive', '--color-olive', 'overlines, labels, mark'],
  ['Meta', '--color-meta', 'captions, meta lines, muted mono'],
];

const typeRows = [
  ['display · 54/1.06 · 600 · -1.5%', 'type-display', 'Pin your scripts'],
  ['h2 · 32/1.15 · 600 · -1%', 'type-h2', 'Get pinchos'],
  ['h3 · 22/1.3 · 600', 'type-h3', 'Rows stay ordered'],
  ['body · 16.5/1.65 · 400', 'type-body', 'Cached values stay close at hand.'],
  ['small · 14/1.6 · 500', 'type-small', 'Build it yourself'],
  ['overline · 12 · 500 · +9% · caps', 'type-overline', 'macOS menu bar utility'],
  ['code · 13.5/1.85 · 400', 'type-code', 'swift build -c release'],
];

const spaces = [4, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32, 48, 64, 96];
---

<BaseLayout title="pinchos web design system" description="The web design system for pinchos." docs>
  <div class="docs-page container container--docs">
    <header class="docs-intro">
      <div class="docs-intro__identity">
        <Mark size={26} label="pinchos mark" />
        <strong>pinchos</strong>
        <span>web design system · 0.1</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="serif-heading">Everything the site is allowed to do.</h1>
      <p class="body-copy">Scope: the website only. The product's own native menu behavior lives in the Swift package — the site quotes the product, never restyles it.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="principles-heading">
      <h2 id="principles-heading" class="serif-heading">1 · Principles</h2>
      <div class="principles-grid">
        <p><strong>Paper, not chrome.</strong> Ivory background, ink text, hairline rules. No gradients, no glass, no dark mode in 0.1.</p>
        <p><strong>The product is the only dark surface.</strong> Menu-bar mockups and code blocks sit on charcoal; nothing else does.</p>
        <p><strong>One accent per block.</strong> Terracotta is interactive, olive is labels. Never both carrying meaning in the same block.</p>
        <p><strong>Write like a README.</strong> Matter-of-fact, lowercase “pinchos”, no exclamation marks, no superlatives.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="mark-heading">
      <h2 id="mark-heading" class="serif-heading">2 · Mark &amp; wordmark</h2>
      <div class="mark-layout">
        <div>
          <div class="mark-specimen raised-card">
            {[96, 48, 24, 16].map((size) => <div class="mark-size"><Mark size={size} label={`pinchos mark at ${size} pixels`} /><span>{size}</span></div>)}
          </div>
          <p class="mono-note">tres pinchos mark. Sticks thicken and heads grow as it shrinks — the same scaling rule as the app icon. Clearspace: one head diameter on all sides.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="lockup raised-card"><Mark size={30} /><span>pinchos</span></div>
          <p class="mono-note">lockup: mark + Bricolage Grotesque 700, always lowercase. Gap = 45% of mark height. Favicon = mark alone on transparent.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mark-rules">
          <div class="overline">rules</div>
          <div>· never recolor or outline the mark</div>
          <div>· never place it inside menu-bar mockups</div>
          <div>· ivory-tile version only for app-icon contexts</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="color-heading">
      <h2 id="color-heading" class="serif-heading">3 · Color</h2>
      <div class="color-grid">
        {colors.map(([name, token, role]) => <div class="color-card">
          <div class="color-card__swatch" style={`background: var(${token})`}></div>
          <div class="color-card__body"><strong>{name}</strong><code>{token}</code><span>{role}</span></div>
        </div>)}
      </div>
      <p class="docs-note">Contrast: Ink on Paper 12.1:1. Link terracotta on Paper is approximately 4.7:1; brand terracotta is decorative or large-display only. Olive is for overlines and marks, never body copy. Derive any new shade from these hues.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="type-heading">
      <h2 id="type-heading" class="serif-heading">4 · Typography</h2>
      <div class="type-family-row">
        <span><b>Source Serif 4</b> - display, H1-H2, feature H3s</span>
        <span><b>Bricolage Grotesque</b> - body, UI, wordmark</span>
        <span><b>IBM Plex Mono</b> - overlines, code, meta</span>
      </div>
      <div class="type-table">
        {typeRows.map(([spec, className, sample]) => <div class="type-row"><code>{spec}</code><span class={className}>{sample}</span></div>)}
        <p>Rules: serif never below 20px · sentence case everywhere · “pinchos” always lowercase, even at line start · technical values use mono.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="spacing-heading">
      <h2 id="spacing-heading" class="serif-heading">5 · Spacing &amp; layout</h2>
      <div class="spacing-layout">
        <div>
          <div class="overline">scale · base 4</div>
          <div class="space-scale">{spaces.map((space) => <div><i style={`height: ${space}px`}></i><code>{space}</code></div>)}</div>
        </div>
        <div class="spacing-rules">
          <div class="overline">rules</div>
          <div>container <code>max-width 1080</code>, side padding 32 · section rhythm 72-96 · gaps from the scale only</div>
          <div>radii: 8 buttons · 10 chips/cards · 12 code &amp; mockups — nothing rounder</div>
          <div>borders <code>1px rgba(43,42,40,.14)</code> · one shadow, product mockups only</div>
          <div>alternate bands: Paper → Paper Raised → Charcoal, at most one charcoal band per page</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="components-heading">
      <h2 id="components-heading" class="serif-heading">6 · Components</h2>
      <div class="component-grid">
        <article class="component-card raised-card">
          <div class="overline">buttons &amp; links</div>
          <div class="component-actions"><Button href="#primary">Primary</Button><Button href="#secondary" variant="secondary">Secondary</Button><a href="#link">Text link</a></div>
          <p>One primary per view. Hover darkens one step; focus ring is 2px Link Terracotta, offset 2. Links underline on paper; nav/footer links skip the underline.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="component-card raised-card">
          <div class="overline">code</div>
          <CodeBlock lines={['swift build -c release']} />
          <p>Block: charcoal, radius 12, ivory text, prompt in dark prompt terracotta, no syntax rainbow. Inline: <code>pinchos.toml</code> — raised chip, mono, 1px line.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="component-card raised-card">
          <div class="overline">product mockups</div>
          <ProductMockup compact />
          <p>The bar is a dark pill with system font. The submenu demonstrates static, cached, action, run-plus-action, and separator rows in declaration order.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="component-card raised-card">
          <div class="overline">note / callout</div>
          <div class="note-callout"><div class="overline">note</div><p>Raised chip with a mono overline. Full 1px border — never a colored left edge.</p></div>
          <p>Overline color by kind: olive for notes, link terracotta for warnings.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="component-card raised-card component-card--wide">
          <div class="overline">menu rows</div>
          <table class="marker-table">
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">row</th><th scope="col">fields</th><th scope="col">behavior</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>static</td><td><code>label</code> + <code>value</code></td><td>read-only text</td></tr>
              <tr><td>cached</td><td><code>label</code> + <code>run</code> + <code>cache</code></td><td>cached value, background refresh</td></tr>
              <tr><td>action</td><td><code>label</code> + <code>action</code></td><td>runs after activation</td></tr>
              <tr><td>run-plus-action</td><td><code>label</code> + <code>run</code> + <code>action</code></td><td>cached value with an action</td></tr>
              <tr><td>separator</td><td><code>separator = true</code></td><td>visual rule only</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
          <p>Rows are ordered exactly as declared. Menu construction never executes a command.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="component-card raised-card component-card--wide">
          <div class="overline">forms</div>
          <div class="form-layout">
            <form class="specimen-form">
              <label for="item-name">Item name</label><input id="item-name" value="codex" />
              <label for="item-command">Command</label><input id="item-command" value="quota-axi --provider codex --json | jq -r '.providers[0].windows[] | select(.label==\"week\") | .percentRemaining'" />
              <label for="item-interval">Interval</label><select id="item-interval"><option>5m</option></select>
              <button type="button" class="button button--primary">Validate</button>
            </form>
            <div class="form-rules"><div class="overline">rules</div><div>· labels above fields, never placeholder-as-label</div><div>· fields use Paper Field fill, 1px border, radius 8, padding 10 12</div><div>· validate before running a new command</div></div>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="component-card raised-card">
          <div class="overline">tabs · tags · kbd</div>
          <div class="tabs"><span class="tabs__active">Overview</span><span>Config</span><span>Changelog</span></div>
          <div class="chips"><code>menu</code><code class="chip-olive">cached</code><code class="chip-terracotta">read-only</code><kbd><span aria-hidden="true">⌘</span><span class="visually-hidden">Command</span></kbd><kbd>C</kbd></div>
          <p>Tabs use a 2px Link Terracotta underline. Tags are mono chips; kbd uses a 2px bottom border.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="component-card raised-card">
          <div class="overline">lists · quote · prev/next</div>
          <ul class="olive-list"><li>unordered — olive dot, hanging, 6px row gap</li><li>ordered — mono olive numerals, zero-padded</li></ul>
          <blockquote>“It behaves like a built-in menu extra.”<cite>— design/README.md</cite></blockquote>
          <div class="pager"><a href="#config">← Config format</a><a href="#menu-rows">Menu rows →</a></div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="voice-heading">
      <h2 id="voice-heading" class="serif-heading">7 · Voice</h2>
      <div class="voice-grid"><div><div class="overline">say</div><p>“pinchos runs the commands you give it.”</p><p>“Cached rows refresh in the background.”</p><p>“Free, open source, native AppKit.”</p></div><div><div class="overline overline--terracotta">don't say</div><p>“Supercharge your workflow!”</p><p>“The ultimate menu bar experience.”</p><p>“A settings dashboard for every preference.”</p></div></div>
      <p class="docs-note">Sentence case, present tense, no exclamation marks, and no promises beyond the documented command and menu-row behavior.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section docs-section--last" aria-labelledby="later-heading">
      <h2 id="later-heading" class="serif-heading">8 · Adding pages later</h2>
      <p class="docs-note docs-note--wide">Every new page reuses the landing nav and footer verbatim. Docs pages: single column, max-width 720, body 16.5/1.65, H2s in serif with 56px top spacing, code blocks per section 6. A changelog or blog gets mono dates in olive and serif titles. If a page needs a component this system doesn't define, add it here first — one page, one new component, maximum.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
